i mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905895"}, {"id": "ed9d99", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905896"}, {"id": "35dbc1", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905897"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905898", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478e"], "concepts": ["6117b76b478ae845c43c6d5a"], "question": {"text": "The correct order of bond dissociation enthalpy of halogens is:"}, "options": [{"id": "290448", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a8905899"}, {"id": "7d0d97", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a890589a"}, {"id": "ec1f3d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a890589b"}, {"id": "699258", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a890589c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a890589d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f9"], "concepts": ["60da9b4f62f042332c5382f0"], "question": {"text": "Choose the correct statements from the following</p><p>A. All group <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math> elements form oxides of general formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>o</mi></math>. Both the types of oxides are acidic in nature.</p><p>B. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is an oxidising agent while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is reducing in nature.</p><p>C. The reducing property decreases from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>S</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>T</mi><mi>e</mi></math> down the group.</p><p>D. The ozone molecule contains five lone pairs of electrons.</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "7edd23", "text": "A and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a890589e"}, {"id": "3cd13b", "text": "B and C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a890589f"}, {"id": "88eb5f", "text": "C and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058a0"}, {"id": "b20b8e", "text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058a1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058a2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4751"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87df"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match List - I with List - II:</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\">List-I (Species)</td>\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" rowspan=\"1\">List-II (Number of lone pairs of electrons on the central atom)</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(a)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(i)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(b)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(ii)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(c)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(iii)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>(d)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>(iv)</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7c5d7b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>iii</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>iv</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058a3"}, {"id": "3a5a43", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>iv</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>iii</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058a4"}, {"id": "4a493e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>iii</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>iv</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058a5"}, {"id": "c140ac", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>iv</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>iii</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058a6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058a7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b6f"], "concepts": ["60e567dd499d1e49588f9cc2"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements :</p><p>Statement I: The pentavalent oxide of group-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math>&nbsp;element, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>, is less acidic than trivalent oxide, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>, of the same element.</p><p>Statement II : The acidic character of trivalent oxide of group <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> elements, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>, decreases down the group.</p><p>In light of the above statements, choose most appropriate answer from the options given below</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "29aafb", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058a8"}, {"id": "50c49c", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058a9"}, {"id": "60930a", "text": "Statement I is false but statement II is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058aa"}, {"id": "0daf89", "text": "Statement I true, but statement II is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058ab"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058ac", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["6117b5e7478ae845c43c5eff"], "concepts": ["6162fbe06ed13040ec8540ec"], "question": {"text": "<p>Which of the following oxoacids of sulphur contains &quot;S&quot; in two different oxidation states?</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "14d520", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058ad"}, {"id": "1ea020", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058ae"}, {"id": "b73e8a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058af"}, {"id": "480ed9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058b0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058b1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478e"], "concepts": ["61adb646dec0c790740ace53"], "question": {"text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> has highest boiling point among hydrogen halides, because it has:"}, "options": [{"id": "c9e902", "text": "lowest dissociation enthalpy", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058b2"}, {"id": "750694", "text": "strongest van der Waals’ interactions", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058b3"}, {"id": "cc627d", "text": "strongest hydrogen bonding", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058b4"}, {"id": "619a47", "text": "lowest ionic character", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058b5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058b6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52ed"], "concepts": ["60e567dd499d1e49588f9cc3"], "question": {"text": "<p>An ammoniacal metal salt solution gives a brilliant red precipitate on addition of dimethylglyoxime. The metal ion is :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e54e7d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058b7"}, {"id": "be3c3c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058b8"}, {"id": "8be098", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058b9"}, {"id": "76731e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058ba"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058bb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f9"], "concepts": ["6162fbdf6ed13040ec853fff"], "question": {"text": "Anomalous behaviour of oxygen is due to its"}, "options": [{"id": "320a99", "text": " Large size and high electronegativity ", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058bc"}, {"id": "09ca1e", "text": "Small size and low electronegativity ", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058bd"}, {"id": "3c2dd3", "text": "Small size and high electronegativity ", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058be"}, {"id": "4a37bc", "text": "Large size and low electronegativity", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058bf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058c0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4751"], "concepts": ["6117b64e478ae845c43c6886"], "question": {"text": "Inert gases have positive electron gain enthalpy. Its correct order is"}, "options": [{"id": "bda04e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Xe</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Kr</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Ne</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>He</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058c1"}, {"id": "5e4956", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>He</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Ne</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Kr</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Xe</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058c2"}, {"id": "aad2a4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>He</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Xe</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Kr</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Ne</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058c3"}, {"id": "29c76b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>He</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Kr</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Xe</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Ne</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058c4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058c5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478e"], "concepts": ["6162fbe26ed13040ec85420a"], "question": {"text": "The correct statement about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msubsup><mi>Cl</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "372ba2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> is trigonal bipyramidal and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msubsup><mi>Cl</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> is tetrahedral.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058c6"}, {"id": "aee591", "text": "Both are isostructural.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058c7"}, {"id": "12a320", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> is square pyramidal and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msubsup><mi>Cl</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> is tetrahedral.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058c8"}, {"id": "f31618", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> is square pyramidal and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msubsup><mi>Cl</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> is square planar.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058c9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058ca", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52ed"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c3"], "question": {"text": "On reaction of Lead Sulphide with dilute nitric acid which of the following is not formed?"}, "options": [{"id": "eb37c3", "text": "Nitric oxide", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058cb"}, {"id": "e3748a", "text": "Nitrous oxide", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058cc"}, {"id": "d56045", "text": "Lead nitrate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058cd"}, {"id": "79ccc3", "text": "Sulphur", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058ce"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058cf", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52f9"], "concepts": ["6162fbdf6ed13040ec853fff"], "question": {"text": "The correct group of halide ions which can be oxidised by oxygen in acidic medium is"}, "options": [{"id": "26c6f1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Br</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo></msup></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058d0"}, {"id": "f5d5ef", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Br</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo></msup></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058d1"}, {"id": "ed3430", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo></msup></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058d2"}, {"id": "c9924d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Br</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo></msup></math> only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058d3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058d4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4797"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4751"], "concepts": ["6117b64e478ae845c43c6886"], "question": {"text": "Give below are two statements:</p><p>Statement-I : Noble gases have very high boiling points.</p><p>Statement-II: Noble gases are monoatomic gases. They are held together by strong dispersion forces. Because of this they are liquefied at very low temperature. Hence, they have very high boiling points.</p><p>In the light of the above statements. choose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "ff37c8", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058d5"}, {"id": "b529ba", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058d6"}, {"id": "f9bd13", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058d7"}, {"id": "762808", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f0cc677dc36a89058d8"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", 